t $F=∇f.$ The function $f$ is called a potential function for $F.$\n\nTo compute the vector field associated with a potential function $f,$ we compute its gradient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy-z))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy-z))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy-z))\\,k \\\\  & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,k \\\\  & =F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field that has $f$ as a potential function is\n\n$$\nF=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,k.\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382704 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382705 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382706 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382707 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382703 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382708 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382703 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382703 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382703 1079 #edb/ref 17592186382705 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382703 1080 #uuid "52aae08c-2f4f-5759-bdb7-0ce12352bc22" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382704 1081 "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,i+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,j-z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,k" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382704 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382704 1084 #uuid "d7a94cea-936d-5e4d-ae19-8ad4604dbaa4" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382705 1081 "y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy-z)\\,k" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382705 1083 #