e statements are true" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382758 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382758 1084 #uuid "503ddc68-3af5-5213-9fd8-6a2cb4ba32d0" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382759 1081 "I only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382759 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382759 1084 #uuid "76db3fd3-a4bd-553b-b654-f4a62a908a7b" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382760 1081 "III only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382760 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382760 1084 #uuid "27d3053a-df29-513e-adea-1bd148282afd" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382761 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382761 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382761 1084 #uuid "30c9ef19-213c-51a2-8c69-ae396f12ec41" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382762 1081 "II only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382762 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382762 1084 #uuid "ef2ae372-8142-5317-9926-83c4534bf4ee" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382763 1068 #edb/ref 17592186382764 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382763 1069 "q-105206" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382763 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382763 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:[-2,2]\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{3}-x)?$\n\n- $f(-1)=f(1)$\n- $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in [-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}$\n- $f$ is not **one-to-one**" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382763 1072 #uuid "b0c99dc3-deba-5ffb-83d8-510a75eea6dd" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382763 1074 "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/86/869be2ef6cb317b81c249b85b0afcbea23178dcf3bb77bb008e69375494439df.png)\n\nA function $f:X\\to Y$ is an injection (also known as *one-to-one*) if *every* element in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(-1)=\\frac{1}{2}((-1)^{3}-(-1))=0$ and $f(1)=\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{3}-1)=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have $f(-1)=f(1)$ but $-1\\ne 1.$ So, it's *not true* that for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $[-2,2],$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since statement II is false, $f$ is not an injection (also known as *one-to-one*).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382765 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382766 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382767 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382768 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382769 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382764 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382764 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382764 1079 #edb/ref 17592186382765 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382764 1080 #uuid "14e32f15-3f83-5df0-8311-8b91106c0d3a" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382765 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382765 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382765 1084 #uuid "34505d93-61ab-54b2-bd41-631e7fe86cf6" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382766 1081 "I only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382766 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382766 1084 #uuid "9ab898b4-f67d-5362-8e83-64c6b4b9871d" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382767 1081 "III only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382767 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382767 1084 #uuid "f9ac8e0c-7ee0-51ed-b2e3-112bcb902015" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382768 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382768 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382768 1084 #uuid "46208dd3-0594-5971-9721-ae700d6ea0ad" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382769 1081 "II only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382769 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382769 1084 #uuid "7e1d71f5-b604-57a9-9570-68db5289aa96" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382770 1068 #edb/ref 17592186382771 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382770 1069 "q-105218" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382770 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382770 1071 "Which of the following functions are injections?\n\n- $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$\n- $g:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- $h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)=(x+1)^{2}$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382770 1072 #uuid "6a4c4299-1d16-58a6-b63b-ffcefd188616" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382770 1074 "A function $f:X\\to Y$ is a **injection** (also known as **one-to-one**) if *every* element in $x$ in $X$ is mapped to a *distinct* element in $Y.$\n\nSymbolically, we can write:\n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ if $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$\n\n- I is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({x}_{1}) & =f({x}_{2}) \\\\ {2}^{{x}_{1}} & ={2}^{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡{2}^{{x}_{1}} & ={log}_{2}⁡{2}^{{x}_{2}} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- II is an injection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{1} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{1}} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{2}} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- III is *not* an injection. For example, $h(0)=1=h(-2),$ but $0\\ne -2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382772 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382773 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382774 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382775 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382771 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382776 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382771 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382771 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382771 1079 #edb/ref 17592186382775 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382771 1080 #uuid "8b429c17-5b26-5fdc-a4e7-7825832bf15f" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382772 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382772 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382772 1084 #uuid "33fd11e0-02ac-54f2-bf8e-fd86f65bf26f" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382773 1081 "I only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382773 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382773 1084 #uuid "907807b7-8592-5a51-8f87-cdfaf42f9303" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382774 1081 "III only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382774 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382774 1084 #uuid "522f005e-6b19-51a7-aabc-8a2ad6b8f2e2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382775 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382775 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382775 1084 #uuid "ef273738-5da3-5881-882b-995b8bbb892e" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382776 1081 "II only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382776 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382776 1084 #uuid "9cf75fd8-5e38-5898-8705-e42afabf9d42" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382777 1068 #edb/ref 17592186382778 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382777 1069 "q-105224" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382777 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382777 1071 "![](images/32/32957c5f0b4eeb76253f9fe812e2025b93a2cd5c65870f5a0b3608ce545dd4c5.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\n- $f$ is a surjection\n- $f$ is an injection\n- $f$ is a bijection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382777 1072 #uuid "db660bb9-e18a-5aa6-8b12-2d9637cff073" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382777 1074 "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, according to the diagram, for every element $y\\in Y,$ we have an arrow from some element $x\\in X$ to it, which means that $f(x)=y.$ So, $f$ is a surjection.\n\n- Statement II is true. As we can see from the diagram, there are no two distinct elements within $X$ that map to the same element in $Y.$ So, for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ contained within the domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since both statements I and II are true, $f$ is a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382779 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382780 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382781 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382782 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382778 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382783 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382778 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382778 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382778 1079 #edb/ref 17592186382780 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382778 1080 #uuid "24cac576-6eca-541f-90a0-57b5aa4e3431" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382779 1081 "None of the statements are true" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382779 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382779 1084 #uuid "9b70deaa-282c-5afd-adea-810a6ceee3dc" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382780 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382780 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382780 1084 #uuid "59aaabbf-93df-5fad-99ef-390a87fba93e" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382781 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382781 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382781 1084 #uuid "466efc04-68cc-5cb3-bcc9-8c69d6dd4f2d" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382782 1081 "I only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382782 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382782 1084 #uuid "c81e5b67-70e8-598c-8964-0be344c1631b" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382783 1081 "II only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382783 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382783 1084 #uuid "413ae4ae-71d1-51be-beb0-c902620af91e" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382784 1068 #edb/ref 17592186382785 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382784 1069 "q-105283" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382784 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382784 1071 "Which of the following functions are bijections?\n\n- $f:{R}^{+}\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$\n- $g:R\\to R$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{3}$\n- $h:Q\\to Q$ defined by $h(x)=|x|$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382784 1072 #uuid "aad509f8-bb58-5f68-8c6d-48ccc6e72f00" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382784 1074 "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\n- I is *not* a bijection because it is not surjective. Remember that the range of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ is $f(x)\\in (0,\\infty )$ for $x\\in {R}^{+}.$ So, for example, there is no value $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-1.$\n\n- II is a bijection. First of all, it is a surjection because $∀\\,y\\in R,$ we can choose an $x\\in R$ such that $g(x)=y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & =y \\\\ {x}^{3} & =y \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[3]{y}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe verify that\n\n$$\ng(x)=g(\\sqrt[3]{y})={(\\sqrt[3]{y})}^{3}=y.\n$$\n\nSecond, it is an injection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({x}_{1}) & =g({x}_{2}) \\\\ {x}_{1}^{3} & ={x}_{2}^{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & ={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause $g$ is both surjective and injective, $g$ is bijective.\n\n- III is *not* a bijection because it is not injective. Notice that $h(-1)=1=h(1),$ while $-1\\ne 1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382785 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382786 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382785 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382787 13194139533455 1