4 #uuid "16d79a23-b8a4-5066-8adc-8969c5a8a7c2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382819 1068 #edb/ref 17592186382820 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382819 1069 "q-105330" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382819 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382819 1071 "![](images/88/8845d8cc2664c92637e06961f1d5c17b98afcb72470d1463fbd58aaf5691ca4c.png)\n\nFor the function $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=(x+1)^{2}-2$, which of the following statements are true?  \n\n- The function is an injection\n- The function is a surjection\n- The function is a bijection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382819 1072 #uuid "ea34001e-7666-5760-9335-3a797f196771" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382819 1074 "Recall that a function $f:X\\to Y$ is \n\n- an injection if $∀\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in X,$ whenever $f({x}_{1})=f({x}_{2}),$ we have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$\n\n- a surjection if $∀\\,y\\in Y,$ $∃\\,x\\in X$ such that $f(x)=y,$\n\n- a bijection if it is both a surjection and an injection.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. There are horizontal lines (such as the one depicted below) that cross the graph of $f(x)$ more than once.\n\n![](images/d6/d6b2a99811341aa07bc3e91df973504fad57ac4a71a38406707b5d311247d61d.png)\n\n        \n\n- Statement II is false. For example, there is not $x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=-4.$ So, $f$ is not a surjection.\n\n- Statement III is false, because the function is not both an injection and a surjection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\"" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382820 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382821 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382820 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382822 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382820 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382823 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382820 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382824 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [1759218