d} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we have ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 0+{x}_{3}=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1-{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1-{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{3}=1,$ we get  \n\n$$\n{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+c=0+1=1.$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382951 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382952 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382953 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382954 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382955 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382950 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382950 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382950 1079 #edb/ref 17592186382952 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382950 1080 #uuid "121a22dc-dff7-5901-89d2-fdc3f56aac76" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382951 1081 "2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382951 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382951 1084 #uuid "075a406a-2607-5dad-8a65-47b8a9f71b37" 13194