sponding to $\\lambda =-3,$ and\n\n- a single $1\\times 1$ block corresponding to $\\lambda =-2.$\n\nTherefore, the columns of $P$ form the following chains: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{J}_{2}(-3) & : & {v}_{2}\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A+3I\\,}{\\to }0 &  \\\\ {J}_{1}(-2) & : & {v}_{3}\\overset{A+2I\\,}{\\to }0 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain that \n\n- the first column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ of the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3,$\n\n- the second column of $P$ corresponds to the vector ${v}_{2}$ such that $(A+3I){v}_{2}={v}_{1}.$\n\nNow, computing $A+3I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+3I & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix equation $(A+3I){v}_{2}={v}_{1}$ is equivalent to the system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has two pivot columns (the $1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the first and second equations, we have ${x}_{1}=1-{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}-1,$ respectively. \n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1-{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{3}=0,$ we get  \n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $2a+b=2\\cdot 1+(-1)=1.$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382958 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382959 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382960 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382961 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382962 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382957 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382957 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382957 1079 #edb/ref 17592186382959 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382957 1080 #uuid "57bbc87f-a7f2-5ebc-9d06-4527c75aaad3" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382958 1081 "2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382958 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382958 1084 #uuid "a1c11575-8d13-5afe-b9fe-79b799dc670c" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382959 1081 "1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382959 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382959 1084 #uuid "f731ec5a-1331-5c82-9c97-f0673498f6ee" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382960 1081 "0" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382960 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382960 1084 #uuid "6513b96e-1050-5b32-b77b-9faaccd220bc" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382961 1081 "-1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382961 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186382961 1084 