55 17592186045585 true] [17592186383061 1074 "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nFor the vector field $F,$ the domain $D={R}^{2},$ and we have \n\n$$\nP=a\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-y),\\,Q=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-y)+1.\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-a\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y),\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y).\n$$\n\nIt's clear that the partial derivatives exist and are continuous on ${R}^{2}.$ Equating the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-a\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y)+a\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) & =0 \\\\ (3+a)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-y) & =0 \\\\ 3+a & =0 \\\\ a & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=-3.$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383063 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383064 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383065 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383066 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383067 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383062 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383062 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383062 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383066 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383062 1080 #uuid "3bcb7611-75f0-57b9-8afb-f4a5ccb4b065" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383063 1081 "3" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383063 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383063 1084 #uuid "bd9d3890-e5fa-57a3-9137-e