13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383143 1084 #uuid "dc595fac-dae6-5410-827a-24f260bf76a7" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383144 1081 "3x-z-5=0" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383144 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383144 1084 #uuid "29783bfa-7d2c-50b4-9f47-577066578c2b" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383145 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383146 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383145 1069 "q-129659" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383145 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383145 1071 "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(3,2,1)=12,\\,{f}_{x}(3,2,1)=4,\\,{f}_{y}(3,2,1)=12,\\,{f}_{z}(3,2,1)=36.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,2,1)$ estimate the value of $f(2.97,2.1,1.04).$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383145 1072 #uuid "6b880160-8e82-545a-ac66-2d0d38f21ec0" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383145 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(3,2,1)+∇f(3,2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-2,z-1⟩ \\\\  & =12+⟨{f}_{x}(3,2,1),{f}_{y}(3,2,1),{f}_{z}(3,2,1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-2,z-1⟩ \\\\  & =12+⟨4,12,36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,y-2,z-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(2.97,2.1,1.04)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=2.97,$ $y=2.1,$ and $z=1.04$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.97,2.1,1.04) & ≈12+⟨4,12,36⟩\\cdot ⟨2.97-3,2.1-2,1.04-1⟩ \\\\  & =12+⟨4,12,36⟩\\cdot ⟨-0.03,0.1,0.04⟩ \\\\  & =12+4(-0.03)+12(0.1)+36(0.04) \\\\  & =12-0.12+1.2+1.44 \\\\  & =14.52\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383147 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383148 1319413953