] [17592186383200 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383200 1084 #uuid "6b9641c2-5c4b-5522-8865-349e9ec14602" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383201 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383202 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383201 1069 "q-130737" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383201 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383201 1071 "Suppose $C$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(C)=-5.$ What is the value of $det(-2C)?$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383201 1072 #uuid "9a5f04aa-dd8a-5322-9e5d-a0849f397bd2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383201 1074 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot C)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-2$ and $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-2C) & =(-2)^{4}\\cdot det(C) \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383202 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383203 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383202 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383204 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383202 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383205 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383202 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383206 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383202 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383207 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383202 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383202 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383202 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383206 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383202 1080 #uuid "92409d8d-b10d-5c4d-a7d1-a42d1b0cfc78" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383203 1081 "-40" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383203 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [1759