] [17592186383225 1084 #uuid "bea9ac5f-6965-5feb-9890-9a84bb8fa9c1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383226 1081 "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{3}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383226 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383226 1084 #uuid "c930d2e4-f0f9-5e23-b593-fbc36215932d" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383227 1081 "{R}_{3}:=-3{R}_{3}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383227 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383227 1084 #uuid "dce12cc1-6fe9-5710-9501-662de6d6ea91" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383228 1081 "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{3}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383228 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383228 1084 #uuid "5c5d3036-4719-5fd7-ba58-918a06722081" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383229 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383230 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383229 1069 "q-131117" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383229 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383229 1071 "For the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{3}yz-xy{z}^{2}$, find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,1).$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383229 1072 #uuid "14180128-1a3b-5df5-945e-e4a1d12a6375" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383229 1074 "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,1)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(1,-2,1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}yz-xy{z}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}yz-xy{z}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{3}yz-xy{z}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}yz-y{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+({x}^{3}z-x{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+({x}^{3}y-2xyz)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(1,-2,1) & =(3(1)^{2}(-2)(1)-(-2)(1)^{2})\\,i+((1)^{3}(1)-(1)(1)^{2})\\,j+((1)^{3}(-2)-2(1)(-2)(1))\\,k \\\\  & =-4\\,i+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-4\\,i+2\\,k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,1).$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383231 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383232 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383233 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383234 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383235 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383230 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383230 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383230 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383235 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383230 1080 #uuid "6d2c4aa2-5988-5483-be94-986ea095a0e4" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383231 1081 "-2\\,j+4\\,k" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383231 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383231 1084 #uuid "ed39b029-85c3-5e97-8954-e0c143d2660e" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383232 1081 "-4\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383232 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383232 1084 #uuid "09fedb26-ce0e-5168-aa47-838277d2a8de" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383233 1081 "4\\,i-k" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383233 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383233 1084 #uuid "f08ae5ee-40c5-51a6-9971-2dada660033f" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383234 1081 "-2\\,i-2\\,j+k" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383234 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383234 1084 #uuid "0e4bca3e-62b0-506e-ab11-64664053f91f" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383235 1081 "-4\\,i+2\\,k" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383235 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383235 1084 #uuid "ec84b4f7-88ba-52da-a5bb-02c8fc23e908" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383236 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383237 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383236 1069 "q-131124" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383236 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383236 1071 "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the surface $4{z}^{2}-4{y}^{2}={x}^{2}-6x+12$ at the point $(2,0,1).$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383236 1072 #uuid "2fb8c052-74b8-5a3f-8748-9c302788bd84" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383236 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{z}^{2}-4{y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 4{z}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+6x & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=4{z}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+6x$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=12.$ \n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(2,0,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(2,0,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(2,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{z}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+6x)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{z}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+6x)j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4{z}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+6x)k \\\\  & =(6-2x)\\,i-8y\\,j+8z\\,k \\\\ ∇f(2,0,1) & =(6-2(2))\\,i-8(0)\\text{ }j+8(1)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+8\\,k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the vector equation of the line that is parallel to $∇f(2,0,1)$ and passes through the point $(2,0,1)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨2,0,1⟩+t\\,∇f(2,0,1)=⟨2,0,1⟩+t\\,⟨2,0,8⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" 13194139533455 175921