}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383315 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383316 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383317 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383318 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383319 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383314 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383314 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383314 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383316 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383314 1080 #uuid "9c8364fd-cb71-5621-b790-1b21e9be9448" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383315 1081 "\\pi " 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383315 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383315 1084 #uuid "1e7ce596-2d30-587f-8420-45e62e13d5dd" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383316 1081 "\\frac{1+\\pi }{e}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383316 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383316 1084 #uuid "877b2fa4-194f-5fc4-8176-fe7bfbedcc56" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383317 1081 "2\\pi e" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383317 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383317 1084 #uuid "8ca68eba-afe1-5148-a902-7b75f1cf86fe" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383318 1081 "e+\\pi " 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383318 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383318 1084 #uuid "625a56ce-727a-5b05-a3f7-9bccf25f5e8b" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383319 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{{e}^{2}}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383319 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383319 1084 #uuid "2f162d22-7bab-5326-997a-02d3e40fadea" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383320 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383321 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383320 1069 "q-132609" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383320 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383320 1071 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Given that the point $P(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1,0)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}y)$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383320 1072 #uuid "d71daf7a-6da8-5e30-8340-64d86d4d3ded" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383320 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 1)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1) & ={f}_{y}(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1)(y-1) \\\\ z-0 & =2(y-1) \\\\ z & =2y-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1,0)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ z=2y-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=2y-2$ (or $2y-z-2=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =j+2\\,k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,1,2⟩.$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383322 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383323 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383324 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383325 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383326 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383321 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383321 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383321 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383323 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383321 1080 #uuid "51a3324e-1ddd-5ca6-b734-63094c92f926" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383322 1081 "⟨0,3,2⟩" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383322 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383322 1084 #uuid "98ed7ce5-304c-5eac-b1cb-5f8c4b4d23e8" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383323 1081 "⟨0,1,2⟩" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383323 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383323 1084 #uuid "4d34dabe-6639-51a1-abc1-40a551267c42" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383324 1081 "⟨0,2,-1⟩" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383324 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383324 1084 #uuid "7f96ce17-18b2-5a3f-8e28-936aabc05996" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383325 1081 "⟨0,1,-3⟩" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383325 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383325 1084 #uuid "d7fe8dda-e437-53fb-9f60-09b8a339e900" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383326 1081 "⟨0,2,3⟩" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383326 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383326 1084 #uuid "650c5858-626f-56bb-bae0-7ffa49b7eab0" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383327 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383328 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383327 1069 "q-133219" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383327 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383327 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =axy-{x}^{2}, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =y-5b{x}^{2}-7, \\\\ {f}_{x}(1,2) & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383327 1072 #uuid "6f003614-2ab7-5d2a-baaf-9e756e649f1d" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383327 1074 "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(axy-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =ax-0 \\\\  & =ax \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-5b{x}^{2}-7) \\\\  & =0-10bx-0 \\\\  & =-10bx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ax & =-10bx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get $b=-\\frac{a}{10}.$ \n\nNow, since ${f}_{x}(1,2)=21$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,2) & =19 \\\\ a\\cdot 2\\cdot 1-{1}^{2} & =19 \\\\ 2a & =20 \\\\ a & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nb=-\\frac{a}{10}=-\\frac{10}{10}=-1.\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383328 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383329 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383328 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383330 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383328 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383331 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383328 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383332 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383328 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383333 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383328 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383328 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383328 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383331 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383328 1080 #uuid "38ca9d30-442a-5239-931b-e67097bf950b" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383329 1081 "a=5,\\,b=-2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383329 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383329 1084 #uuid "e2d1a520-147a-5e42-a71f-f13ec416c16e" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383330 1081 "a=25,\\,b=4" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383330 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383330 1084 #uuid "82badd18-ae1b-5057-9720-0da1dafcb230" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383331 1081 "a=10,\\,b=-1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383331 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383331 1084 #uuid "7f082fa4-44de-511a-800a-20bfa9e90116" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383332 1081 "a=2,\\,b=-5" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383332 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383332 1084 #uuid "73e5037f-6d39-5e83-a485-ac3936e3d687" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383333 1081 "a=10,\\,b=5" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383333 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383333 1084 #uuid "faf48435-ce72-5f22-b313-b5e0e6df7cc2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383334 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383335 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383334 1069 "q-133262" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383334 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383334 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=6{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=6xy$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=15{x}^{2}-y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=8y+x$\n- ${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-3{y}^{2}$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383334 1072 #uuid "017164c5-337a-58b5-8e66-674d944a6841" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383334 1074 "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2})=6y \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6xy)=6y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(15{x}^{2}-y)=-1 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8y+x)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)=0 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2})=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$,  the third pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533455 