7592186383436 1084 #uuid "f1836749-28a7-5fbd-bd3f-d78ad98340b1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383438 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383437 1069 "q-139554" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383437 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383437 1071 "![](images/63/63d5de8c08559ecc88b4fd7e2184204a1e6ea2f8a9e8ca6af7959e2354876e3f.png)\n\nA $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ maps the unit circle ${x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}$ from ${R}^{2}$ onto an ellipse in ${R}^{2}.$ The corresponding ellipse and its principal axes are depicted in the diagram above. Given that ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A,$ which of the following is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $9$ of ${A}^{T}A?$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383437 1072 #uuid "caf843b3-f2a1-5bdc-8d57-74ed37aa0fe2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383437 1074 "Suppose $A$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix. Let \n\n$$\n{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\,…,{v}_{n}}\n$$\n\nbe an *orthonormal* basis of ${R}^{n}$ consisting of the eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}A$ with corresponding eigenvalues \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}\\ge {\\lambda }_{2}\\ge …\\ge {\\lambda }_{n}.\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{1},$\n\n- ${\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}$ is the length of $A{v}_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nIn our example, we see that\n\n- $||A{v}_{1}||=5={\\sigma }_{1},$ which means that ${\\lambda }_{1}={5}^{2}=25,$ and\n\n- $||A{v}_{2}||=3={\\sigma }_{2},$ which means that ${\\lambda }_{2}={3}^{2}=9.$\n\nTherefore, an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=9$ of ${A}^{T}A$ is ${v}_{2}.$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383439 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383440 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383441 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383442 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383438 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383443 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383438 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383438 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383438 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383440 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383438 1080 #uuid "5c7c6fc9-8fb7-527f-ae85-2cdf815c3fbb" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383439 1081 "{v}_{1}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383439 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383439 1084 #uuid "be3ba996-d9c0-57d3-95cc-5f43b21decb6" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383440 1081 "{v}_{2}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383440 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383440 1084 #uuid "4bbea375-60a4-5dc4-b6be-dd9b80d209fb" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383441 1081 "A{v}_{2}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383441 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383441 1084 #uuid "85175ea8-b77f-56c3-83e4-10dd48da9dc3" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383442 1081 "A{v}_{1}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383442 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383442 1084 #uuid "98ae820c-445e-5ef8-bf8b-2b43811699d7" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383443 1081 "A{A}^{T}{v}_{1}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383443 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383443 1084 #uuid "0a9af6f2-c869-5f00-9c07-d01d9bfe39e5" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383444 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383445 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383444 1069 "q-13960" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383444 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383444 1071 "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383444 1072 #uuid "47ab9fdb-d1cf-5779-9976-0f46f4759b42" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383444 1074 "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,1\\,|=1\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383445 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383446 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383445 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383447 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383445 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383448 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383445 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383449 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383445 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383450 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383445 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383445 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383445 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383448 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383445 1080 #uuid "27f4a562-75c5-5a75-8ff5-ca7a8bf79922" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383446 1081 "20" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383446 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383446 1084 #uuid "d0f71e4c-99fc-528e-ba79-3df352bb024e" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383447 1081 "2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383447 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383447 1084 #uuid "d7abfc77-d448-5303-8b54-d97fd1a2d5c5" 131