gned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3u-5v \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383507 1072 #uuid "1d4d00b9-f07a-56e5-8c62-1dc781808a7b" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383507 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=3u-5v$ and $y(u,v)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$  \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =3 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-5 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{u+v} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\frac{1}{u+v}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{u+v} & \\frac{1}{u+v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (\\frac{1}{u+v})-(-5)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{u+v}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{u+v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383509 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383510 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383511 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383512 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383508 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383513 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383508 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383508 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383508 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383509 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383508 1080 #uuid