ue] [17592186383737 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383737 1084 #uuid "5f51e378-c5ec-546a-ac76-e555b76bf155" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383738 1081 "k=1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383738 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383738 1084 #uuid "7786afa2-d20c-5f4d-870d-9aaca9c1f770" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383739 1081 "k\\ge 1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383739 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383739 1084 #uuid "67a498a9-3adc-5b0a-b0c2-7132cec48d89" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383741 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383746 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383751 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383756 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383762 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383766 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383769 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383774 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383779 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1069 "q-182660" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1071 "Prove that ${\\sum }_{i=2}^{n}{3}^{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{n+1}-9)$ using mathematical induction." 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1072 #uuid "47924cc9-86e4-56c8-99ad-4963d8cfd018" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383740 1074 "A variant of the principle of induction states the following: Let ${n}_{0}$ be an integer. Suppose we have a sequence of mathematical statements $P({n}_{0}),P({n}_{0}+1),P({n}_{0}+2),…,$ where\n\n- $P({n}_{0})$ is true, and\n\n- $P(k)⇒P(k+1)$ for every natural number $k\\ge {n}_{0}.$\n\nThen, $P(n)$ is true for every natural number $n\\ge {n}_{0}.$\n\nIn this case, the general statement $P(n)$ we're required to prove is the following:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=2}^{n}{3}^{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{n+1}-9)\n$$\n\nWe start by proving the so-called base case, $P(2).$ To do this, we substitute $n=2$ into both the left-hand side and right-hand side and show that they're equal:\n\nWe proceed using induction on $n.$\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove our statement is true for the base case $n=2.$\nFor the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=2}^{2}{3}^{i}={3}^{2}=9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for the right-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{2+1}-9)=\\frac{1}{2}(18)=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, our statement is true for $n=2.$\n\nNext, we state our inductive hypothesis. Here, we assume that the given statement is true for some $n=k\\ge 2.$ \n\nDue to the base case, we already *know* that the statement is true for *some* value of $k,$ namely $k=2,$ so this assumption is valid.\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n=k\\ge 2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=2}^{k}{3}^{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{k+1}-9).\n$$\n\nWe must show that $P(k)⇒P(k+1).$ Let's start by writing down $P(k+1).$ This is the first part of the so-called **inductive step**, so let's write that, too.\n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=2}^{k+1}{3}^{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{k+2}-9).\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThe idea is to rewrite the left-hand side of $(∗)$ *using the inductive hypothesis* and apply algebraic techniques to show that this equals the right-hand side.\n\nWhen proving sums of finite series using induction, the key to unlocking the proof is to write the last term on its own, as follows: \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{k+1}{a}_{i}=({\\sum }_{i=1}^{k}{a}_{i})+{a}_{k+1}\n$$\n\nLet's apply this technique in this case:\n\nWe write\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=2}^{k+1}{3}^{i}=({\\sum }_{i=2}^{k}{3}^{i})+{3}^{k+1}.\n$$\n\nBy the inductive hypothesis, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=2}^{k}{3}^{i})+{3}^{k+1} & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{k+1}-9)+{3}^{k+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {3}^{k+1}-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {3}^{k+2}-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{k+2}-9),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nas required.\n\nSince we've shown that the left-hand side of $(∗)$ equals the right-hand side, our proof is complete. So let's write down our conclusion. \n\nTherefore, by the principle of induction, ${\\sum }_{i=2}^{n}{3}^{i}=\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{n+1}-9)$ is true for all $n\\ge 2.$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383742 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383743 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383744 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383745 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383741 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383741 1077 "field-9" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383741 1079 #edb/ref 17592186383745 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383741 1080 #uuid "79f717f0-6afd-5753-a85c-b00110d1b685" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383742 1081 "n=1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383742 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383742 1084 #uuid "247b5842-e81b-5592-aa17-dc9608217c0a" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383743 1081 "n=2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383743 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383743 1084 #uuid "44a29b00-c48d-5e69-ae64-9206473fad73" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383744 1081 "n\\ge 1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186383744 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 1759218604558