valuate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\frac{2(0)}{(0)^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{1+(0)^{2}} & 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), so the system is almost linear at ${x}^{∗}.$\n\nTo find the eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix, we write down the characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1,2}=2,\\text{ }3.$\n\nFinally, since we both have two real and positive eigenvalues, our equilibrium is an $\\text{unstable}$ $\\text{source}.$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385229 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385230 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385229 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385231 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385229 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385229 1077 "field-1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385229 1079 #edb/ref 17592186385230 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385229 1080 #uuid "d4b35b6b-b458-56d6-adbd-80469db5e2d7" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385230 1081 "unstable" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385230 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385230 1084 #uuid "e1ecf80d-01dc-5d5d-be6c-c24a533865a7" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385231 1081 "asymptotically stable" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385231 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385231 1084 #uuid "3e476f21-3f14-57f8-89de-7cc24c8619cf" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385232 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385233 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385232 10