\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385448 1072 #uuid "6f2538da-8d51-59ef-9c88-dd06d7af1438" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385448 1074 "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3}.\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385450 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385451 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385452 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385453 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385454 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385449 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385449 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385449 1079 #edb/ref 17592186385453 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385449 1080 #uuid "36b4251d-aea0-541f-9df1-43c7caac3dd1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385450 1081 "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3}" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385450 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385450 1084 #uuid "eef6e93d-f65c-5ac8-a313-118c028fcea5" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385451 1081 "{R}