5754 1074 "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyy}(x,y,z) & ={f}_{yxy}(x,y,z) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{yx}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y\\sqrt{\\frac{{z}^{3}}{x}}+3{z}^{3}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{y}}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{{z}^{3}}{x}}+3{z}^{3}\\sqrt{x}(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{{z}^{3}}{x}}-\\frac{3}{2}{z}^{3}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{{y}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point  $(2,2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyy}(2,2,2) & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{(2)^{3}}{(2)}}-\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{3}\\sqrt{\\frac{(2)}{(2)^{3}}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4-6 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385756 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385757 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385758 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385759 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385760 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385755 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385755 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385755 1079 #edb/ref 17592186385759 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385755 1080 #uuid "a77c5567-cf99-56d1-b14b-dfbb7bd4a79a" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385756 1081 "1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385756 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385756 1084 #uuid "0d1a643b-a893-567e-911e-141f6c6ff871" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385757 1081 "4" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385757 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385757 1084 #uuid "bbd42e7e-ccb9-5de0-94e7-6a5