he domain $X,$ if $f({x}_{1})$ and $f({x}_{2})$ are equal, then we must have ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ As a result, $f$ is an injection.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, since statement I is false,  $f$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385775 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385776 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385775 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385777 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385775 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385778 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385775 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385779 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385775 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385780 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385775 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385775 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385775 1079 #edb/ref 17592186385780 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385775 1080 #uuid "9179f998-6f44-58a9-800b-79c989241d78" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385776 1081 "None of the statements are true" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385776 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385776 1084 #uuid "22c06214-2610-5c0b-af4c-76319cd294f2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385777 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385777 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385777 1084 #uuid "9c4c7672-15c0-508f-99b1-e2ad662ac84e" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385778 1081 "I only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385778 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385778 1084 #uuid "f141b7df-d2b4-5a9a-b43c-9d096a0472a7" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385779 1081 "III only" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385779 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385779 1084 #uuid 