[17592186385827 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385827 1084 #uuid "89b7a97c-5e0d-568a-a37e-3afcc24903a9" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385828 1081 "-4" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385828 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385828 1084 #uuid "2e794247-0a2b-5907-81d1-84fb679377e1" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385829 1081 "-2" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385829 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385829 1084 #uuid "a56a376d-c68d-584d-9779-8ed68890f0a3" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385830 1068 #edb/ref 17592186385831 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385830 1069 "q-94748" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385830 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385830 1071 "Let $f(x,y)=y{x}^{2},$ where $x=ts$ and $y=s-t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385830 1072 #uuid "cddd99f6-007e-52c0-bac7-f496a002a8cf" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385830 1074 "![](images/11/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(ts)(s-t)=2t{s}^{2}-2s{t}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(ts)^{2}={t}^{2}{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =s, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =(2t{s}^{2}-2s{t}^{2})(s)+({t}^{2}{s}^{2})(-1) \\\\  & =2t{s}^{3}-2{s}^{2}{t}^{2}-{t}^{2}{s}^{2} \\\\  & =2t{s}^{3}-3{t}^{2}{s}^{2} \\\\  & =t{s}^{2}(2s-3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385831 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385832 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385831 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385833 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385831 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385834 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385831 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385835 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385831 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385836 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385831 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385831 1077 "selection" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385831 1079 #edb/ref 17592186385836 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385831 1080 #uuid "722f5fc1-8625-5de3-b976-ddcdf5183ff0" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385832 1081 "ts({t}^{2}-3ts+2{s}^{2})" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385832 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385832 1084 #uuid "010a1725-78d9-5ef6-976d-66b572c1b87d" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385833 1081 "s{t}^{2}(s-2t)" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385833 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385833 1084 #uuid "3a12b2ee-d263-5ffd-96bf-c7a89479c594" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385834 1081 "t({s}^{2}+s+1)" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385834 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385834 1084 #uuid "cd01d3dd-a324-5561-83a5-466a5fba3616" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385835 1081 "ts(1+ts)(1-st)" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385835 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385835 1084 #uuid "bc3eb310-caaa-5a1e-9eea-e12deb4203bb" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385836 1081 "t{s}^{2}(2s-3t)" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385836 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385836 1084 #uuid "39c971fc-9574-59c2-93dc-706cf5f69912" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385837 1068 #edb/ref 17592186385838 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385837 1069 "q-94808" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385837 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385837 1071 "Let $Y$ be the set of all ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$  such that $x+y\\le 3.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385837 1072 #uuid "96e3d27f-a6f3-58f8-a748-ec53b79d0713" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385837 1074 "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because **multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed.** *  \n\nFor example, $(1,1)\\in Y$ because $1+1=2\\le 3.$ However, if we add the components of $2\\cdot (1,1)=(2,2),$ we get $2+2=4>3.$ So, $2\\cdot (1,1)\\notin Y.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- The zero element in $Y$ is $(0,0).$ $✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is commutative. $\\,✓$" 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385839 13194139533455 17592186045585 true] [17592186385838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186385840 13194139533455 17